    {
      "id": "caravan-jor",
      "name": "Jor Sandline",
      "species": "Human",
      "gender": "Male",
      "age": 39,
      "occupation": "Caravan Master",
      "category": "travelers",
      "tags": [
        "caravan",
        "routes",
        "deals"
      ],
      "description": "Jor holds down a caravan yard with callused competence and open ears.",
      "biography": "Jor did not plan to become the neighborhood's go-to caravan master, yet a caravan yard made the choice stick. Now 39, the Human measures success in quiet evenings and unpaid favors returned. He pays in mixed coin to learn who notices, and keeps the route book bound in camel hide the way a confessor keeps secrets. Deals with Orrin; uses Skog's stables; hires Jab. Hope pulls one way—secure Orrin's spice contract exclusively—while caution pulls the other because of losing a season to bandits or tariffs. Offered Jab double to deliver to the mill without a waybill copy.",
      "personality": "Warm with regulars, curt with wasters; pays in mixed coin to learn who notices.",
      "motivation": "Secure enough ground to secure Orrin's spice contract exclusively.",
      "secret": "Quietly arranging matters around this problem: Offered Jab double to deliver to the mill without a waybill copy.",
      "rumor": "A smugglers' mark was seen near a caravan yard on a night Jor worked late.",
      "voice": "Polite public voice; sharper private asides when trust appears.",
      "appearance": "Looks like someone who sleeps lightly; distinctive detail is the route book bound in camel hide.",
