      "description": "Familiar face at inn common rooms along the road; useful, stubborn, and hard to surprise.",
      "biography": "Rilo learned the hard corners of settlement life by working them as a traveling minstrel based out of inn common rooms along the road. At 27, the Half-Elf has a map of loyalties written in calluses rather than ink. Day after day he collects rumors the way others collect coins, and the cape lined with song scraps marks his place in the room. Sometimes rooms with Nessa; carries news. His north star is to be hired by Dame Orla for a full season. The shadow at his heels is singing the wrong satire in the wrong hall. Heard sailors say Nedda's barge 'rides light and smells bright'.",
