      "description": "The river sailor people recommend when they actually want the job finished.",
      "biography": "People looking for a reliable river sailor are often sent to Tem, who claims river landings and flatboats as familiar ground. At 34, this Human has learned to watch hands before faces. He reads water the way scholars read books; neighbors joke that he would miss a festival before misplacing the rope calluses like badges. Works docks with Mael; cleaner than Nedda. He is saving courage and coin alike to captain his own flatboat next year, while trying not to let fog collisions near the mill race decide the ending. Refused to tow Nedda after smelling her 'grain'.",
